<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM HIKES GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES THURS.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM HIKES GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES THURS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) said in a statement that gasoline prices will be raised by 0.70 drachmas per litre. Also, diesel prices will go up by 3.00 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday and for one week.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after higher world gasoline prices, up by $2.4 per metric tonne, higher diesel prices, up by $12.0 per metric tonne and a higher dollar/drachma parity, it said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
